\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Love divine! what hast Thou done?
\par The immortal God hath died for me!
\par The Father's co-eternal Son
\par Bore all my sins upon the tree;
\par The immortal God for me hath died!
\par My Lord, my Love is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Behold Him, all ye that pass by,
\par The bleeding Prince of life and peace!
\par Come, sinners, see your Maker die,
\par And say, was ever grief like His?
\par Come, feel with me His blood applied;
\par My Lord, my Love is crucified:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Is crucified for me and you,
\par To bring us rebels back to God:
\par Believe, believe the record true,
\par Ye all are bought with Jesu's blood,
\par Pardon for all flows from His side:
\par My Lord, my Love is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then let us sit beneath His Cross,
\par And gladly catch the healing stream,
\par All things  for Him account but loss,
\par And give up all our hearts to Him;
\par Of nothing think or speak beside:
\par My Lord, my Love is crucified.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
